# Cursor rules

**Before making any change, read and follow
`.claude/skills/project-development/SKILL.md`** — the authoritative workflow for
this repo (also enforced by `.cursor/rules/project-development.mdc`,
`alwaysApply: true`). [CLAUDE.md](CLAUDE.md) carries the standing rules and the
doc index; it is the canonical agent doc.

The rules that must hold in every change, restated here because they are the
ones that cost real damage:

- NEVER commit secrets — reference them from `ExternalSecret` manifests.
- NEVER push to `main` — branch → {{ change_request }}, always.
- NEVER `kubectl apply` / `helm upgrade` to deploy — Flux owns Kubernetes state;
  preview with `kustomize build kubernetes/flux`, deploy by merging.
- Containers stay non-root with a read-only root filesystem; no `latest` tags.
- Stay within this repo's single namespace.
- Run `task lint` before opening a {{ change_request }}.
